    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d658">

                <pb facs="0818" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg708"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3320: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Forbes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-26T17:00:00-05:00">December 26, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>278. Your 280, December 26, 4 p.m., last paragraph. On December 23 the Department
                    telegraphed to the American Consul at Geneva<anchor n="8" xml:id="d658-f1"/> the
                    text of the opening and the concluding paragraphs of the statement telegraphed
                    to you in Department’s 273, December 22, 9 p.m.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d658-f2"/>
                    and requested that the Consul inform the Secretary General of the League thereof
                    in confidence.</p>
                <p>If you deem it advisable, you may give French Ambassador in strict confidence a
                    copy of whole statement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
